# tally 2.1.8 (L §4.4; the third turn's non-blocking note from group 2's fix review): days_between(wa, wa) names one
# window twice, taken with its own name once, so it is 0 on every day it can take (z1), as wa == wa is true (z4)
# and windows each prints it plain (z2); two windows stay the hole (z3). 4651a48f printed z1 as the hole.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place pot: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place jar: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wb: date
input m1: money PLN
input m2: money PLN
input dfix: date
input wa: date

move oa: transfers
  on wa
  leg cash from pot to jar amount m1

move ob: transfers
  on dfix
  leg cash from world to pot amount m2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  dfix = 2026-01-01 "s"
  wb = window(2026-04-07, 2026-04-12) "s"
  m1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  m2 = 30.00 PLN "s"
  wa = window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) "s"
  opening[pot] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[jar] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask z1: days_between(wa, wa)
ask z2: days_between(wa, wa)
ask z3: days_between(wa, wb)
ask z4: wa == wa
=== expect
z1: 0
  cut 2026-01-01
z2: 0
  cut 2026-01-01
z3: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for a print" (wa)
  cut 2026-01-01
z4: true
  cut 2026-01-01
